  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_049 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 accuracy. All four scvi_n200+transformer+multiprofile combinations have been tested, confirming transformer aggregation provides a ~2% boost over avgpool and weighted fusion slightly outperforms concat. The remaining untested multimodal multiprofile configurations are dominated by scgpt or pca_n2000 RNA encoders, both of which showed substantially lower performance (0.542 and 0.586 respectively). Question: config_023 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) tests whether the transformer aggregation benefit generalizes across RNA encoders—i.e., whether scgpt's poor performance with avgpool (0.542) is partly due to the aggregation method rather than the encoder itself. Why this is the best use: Among all remaining untested configurations, config_023 has the highest potential ceiling (best image encoder + best aggregation method) and directly addresses the key architectural uncertainty about whether transformer aggregation is encoder-agnostic. While unlikely to surpass 0.725 given scgpt's large gap, it provides the most scientifically informative result with the final two experiments remaining, and no other untested configuration offers a more plausible path to improvement."
}

